# Kept out of the build context.
#
# There was no .dockerignore at all, and the Dockerfile does COPY . . -- so
# every build read the repo-root .env (service role key, JWT secret, Stripe
# secret, Resend key, cron secret), frontend/.env.local, and the keys/
# directory into the image. The multi-stage build meant those layers were not
# in the final image, but they were present during the build and one of them,
# frontend/.env.local, was baked into the static bundle that does ship.
#
# Config now arrives as explicit build args and runtime env instead. Nothing
# secret needs to be in the context, so nothing secret is allowed in it.

# Secrets and local config.
#
# The ** forms are load-bearing. Docker matches these against the whole
# context-relative path, so a bare `.env.*` covers only the repository root --
# it would NOT have excluded frontend/.env.local, which is the single file that
# was actually being compiled into the shipped bundle.
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
keys/
**/keys/
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
client_secret*.json
**/client_secret*.json

# Build output and dependencies -- reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image,
# and copying them in is both slower and a source of host/container mismatch.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
build/
src/tvlc/static/
frontend/dist/

# Repository and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
.vercel/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
*.log

# Large media that the image does not serve
*.mp4
*.mp3
*.asd
*.zip
uploads/
easter-egg-songs/
scratch/
worker/
docs/
tests/
